[00:35.27]Conversation One
[00:37.01]M: Hey, do you have a minute£¿ 
[00:39.28]I'd like to discuss something with you.
[00:41.75]W: Sure, what's on your mind£¿
[00:43.89]M: Well, I can't decide whether we should buy a place or just rent first when we move to San Francisco. 
[00:50.00]Both seem to have their pros and cons, and neither is obviously better.
[00:54.32]W: I agree. Renting means no responsibility for repairs or maintenance. 
[01:00.25]If something breaks, we just call the landlord and they handle it.
[01:04.65]M: Exactly. And we'd have fixed monthly costs, no surprise fees for a new roof or plumbing issues.
[01:12.05]Plus, we could use the gym and pool if we rent in an apartment complex.
[01:16.60]W: True, but renting has downsides too. 
[01:20.17]We'd have to follow strict rules, like no painting walls, maybe no pets, and limits on how long guests can stay.
[01:28.38]M: That's a good point. 
[01:29.81]Buying gives us freedom to remodel the kitchen or change the flooring anytime we want.
[01:34.98]W: But buying also means we're responsible for all repairs¡ªelectrical, plumbing, everything. Those costs add up quickly and unexpectedly.
[01:45.53]M: Right. And don't forget Homeowner Association fees on top of the mortgage. 
[01:50.67]If something major happens, the Homeowner Association might charge us extra. 
[01:55.80]That could be expensive and unplanned.
[01:58.31]W: Plus, if we want to move, we'd have to sell the unit first. 
[02:02.80]That's not very flexible, especially since we're new to the city and don't know which neighborhoods we like.
[02:10.42]M: So you're leaning toward renting£¿ 
[02:12.27]You make good points about flexibility and unexpected costs.
[02:16.01]W: Given our limited budget right now, renting seems safer. 
[02:20.71]We can always buy later once we know the area better and save up more for a down payment.
[02:27.35]M: You're probably right. 
[02:28.77]Let's rent first, save up, and then look into buying in a year or two when we're more settled.
[02:34.28]W: Sounds like a good plan. 
[02:36.08]I'll start looking at rental listings online tonight and compare a few complexes near your new office.
