[18:21.83]Recording Two
[18:23.56]Water is essential to our daily lives, and staying hydrated is crucial for maintaining good health. 
[18:29.81]Many people carry water bottles with them to have access to clean water wherever they go. 
[18:35.41]It's a convenient option that may be more environmentally friendly than disposable plastic water bottles. 
[18:41.44]You might not realize that your reusable water bottle could harbor harmful bacteria or viruses. 
[18:47.35]If you're frequently using a bottle, it's important to understand the risks of a dirty bottle and the steps you can take to keep it clean. 
[18:55.33]Improperly cleaned water bottles can increase the risk of food-borne illness. 
[18:59.94]Older adults and young children may be at particular risk if they drink from dirty water bottles.
[19:06.28]Used and unwashed water bottles can pose serious risks to your health, according to the International Association for Food Protection.
[19:14.66]So, what can you do to properly clean your water bottle£¿ 
[19:18.66]Review your bottle's manufacturer guidelines for tips on proper cleaning. 
[19:23.10]For example, some water bottles can be placed in the dishwasher, but many popular aluminum bottles cannot. 
[19:30.55]Also, mind the smaller parts that may need to be disassembled before washing. 
[19:35.70]In addition to hot water and dish soap, consider using a small bottle brush to cleanse your bottle thoroughly. 
[19:42.51]When washing the bottle, don't forget about the straw. 
[19:45.52]Straws can be particularly challenging to clean. 
[19:48.72]Try using a straw brush to clean the inside of your straw. 
[19:52.46]If you don't have a straw brush, add a tiny drop of soap to one end of the straw and run a bit of water through it. 
[19:59.20]After cleaning your straw with soap and water, you may be able to sterilize it by boiling it in hot water. 
[20:05.67]All in all, to have a clean bottle means that you need to make it a habit to clean your water bottle daily, especially if you use it regularly or fill it with liquids other than water. 
[20:16.90]Regular cleaning will help prevent the accumulation of bacteria and ensure that your water stays fresh and safe to drink. 
[20:24.39]Finally, to minimize the risk of cross-contamination, it is best to avoid sharing your water bottle with others. 
[20:31.17]This is particularly important during flu or cold seasons or if someone is already sick.
[20:37.00]By understanding the dangers of dirty water bottles and following simple cleaning practices, you can maintain health, prevent illness, and enjoy the benefits of staying hydrated. 
