[21:57.28]Precaution is better than cure. 
[21:59.94]This is a quote that fits perfectly when it comes to insurance. 
[22:04.56]You might have researched a lot about life insurance and health insurance policies, but have you ever thought about important things before investing in a car insurance policy£¿ 
[22:15.91]There are some common mistakes to avoid when buying car insurance.
[22:20.88]When purchasing car insurance online, check whether the company is authorized or not. 
[22:26.66]This can be done by visiting the authority or government website. 
[22:31.54]You can also look for the insurer's social media pages to see if they're genuine and read client reviews. 
[22:39.07]It's also a good idea to see if any complaints or enforcement proceedings have been filed against the company you're considering.
[22:47.63]When it comes to insurance coverage, be aware that the goal of insurance is to provide financial security in case of any adversity. 
[22:57.53]If you choose third-party coverage, for example, you will be protected against losses, damage, or deaths caused by third parties. 
[23:06.98]However, because the insurer would not compensate you for your car, you will be responsible for your damage and losses. 
[23:15.49]The idea is to strike a balance between buying too much and too little insurance.
[23:21.13]Add-ons provide more coverage and come at an extra cost. 
[23:25.70]Add-ons can improve your claim payout. 
[23:28.58]Purchasing too many add-ons might significantly raise your premium. 
[23:33.83]On the other side, if you don't opt for any, you can end up with insufficient coverage. 
[23:40.22]You must first assess your insurance requirements before making a decision. 
[23:45.20]If you drive your car every day and are concerned about what to do if it breaks down in the middle of nowhere, a Roadside Assistance Add-on is necessary.
[23:56.08]Finally, you should never lie in any circumstances. 
[24:00.51]Whether seeking a quotation or filing a claim, don't lie to your car insurance provider because it will only bring you more harm than good. 
[24:09.90]In the event of an accident, your application for coverage may be rejected, and your insurer may be obliged to terminate your policy. 
[24:20.03]When it comes to the application process or filing a claim, be truthful and straightforward. 
[24:26.89]Provide all relevant information, such as the car's age, claim history, previous accidents, engine modifications, and so on. 
[24:36.94]The goal is to avoid providing the insurance company with a justification to deny any claims. 
